`,s.jsxs(a.p,{children:['Think about the heater in your room. You turn a knob to say what you want ("I want it warm"), something happens inside the heater, and the room temperature changes. Three things are involved: what you ',s.jsx(a.strong,{children:"ask for"}),", the ",s.jsx(a.strong,{children:"device"})," that acts, and what you ",s.jsx(a.strong,{children:"get"}),". Control engineering is the study of how to make what you get match what you asked for, reliably, even when the world interferes (somebody opens a window, the heater ages, the outside temperature drops)."]}),`
